# PROLOGUE — "Soundcheck", part 3: the Champion, the song, the screams and the Bellshell.
# Canon: the storyboard doc (v2). No Hush and no Nocturne anywhere in the prologue: the threat tonight is maddened monsters.
# Leagues Soprano speaks grand, rhythmic and slightly too loud, like a sermon at a jazz club.

@scene prologue.champion
# PLOT: Mama Dee tries to throw out the freeloader; Leagues names Rex the Champion of All Peoples, then plays "Burn Forever" and tells the Canticle.
# CHARACTER: Rex's delight; the room's disbelief; Roxy's "No offence, Eddar"; Eddar's grace in being overlooked. The prophecy is shown, never announced.
@bgm wyvern_soundcheck
@cam focus leagues
NARRATOR: Back inside. Mama Dee stands over the corner booth, arms folded.
MAMA DEE [angry]: Last time, sugar. You buy a drink, or you walk.
STRANGER: I do not drink. I listen.
MAMA DEE: Listening's a two-drink minimum.
STRANGER: Then I shall listen for free.
MAMA DEE: Rex, honey. Throw this freeloader out.
REX [smug]: On it.
@cmd move_npc rex 4.7 1.4
NARRATOR: He cracks his knuckles and slides across the floor like he's on rails.
@sfx organ
@fx eye_flash leagues
@cam shake
NARRATOR: Leagues rises. His eyes blaze white, and from nowhere comes one low organ chord. The whole bar hears it.
STRANGER: You.
REX: ...Me?
STRANGER: The pauldron. The jaw. The terrible, magnificent hair. It is you. The Champion of All Peoples. The Hero of Legend, as the Canticle calls him.
REX: ...I'm the Hero of Champions?
STRANGER: It is you, and it can be no one else. You are the great One, the Champion of All Peoples, the Hero of Legend that the Canticle foretold millennia ago!
REX [smile]: Whoa, whoa, whoa. Finally, somebody says it.
@cam focus gil
GIL: How much did he pay you, pal?
MAMA DEE: Rex Valor, if you hired a mime to flatter you in my bar, you're paying his tab.
REX: Rex didn't hire nobody! ...Rex should've, though. This is great.
REX [smug]: Hero of All Champions, Adder. Of ALL of 'em. Princesses dig champions, right? That's like the main thing they dig.
EDDAR: In every story I've read, yes. Though seldom for long.
@cam focus spike
SPIKE: Saving the world. From what, his reflection?
LULU: Is it like the festival? Does he have to punch a meteor?
@cam focus roxy
ROXY [angry]: Oh, PLEASE. Rex? Champion of All Peoples? Eddar makes a more believable champion than Rex, sheesh. No offence, Eddar.
EDDAR: None taken. A champion is the one man a frightened world agrees to stand behind. I'd make a poor wall, Roxy. Rex at least has the width.
@cam focus leagues
? "You told me to piss off." -> told {if:seen.prologue.leagues>=2}
? Say nothing. -> song
* told
EDDAR: You told me to piss off.
STRANGER: I did. You didn't. Remember that.
* song
STRANGER: You doubt. Good. Doubt is a rest in the music. It makes the next note louder.
@flag p.leagues_song
@cmd move_npc leagues 4.6 0.6
@cmd move_npc leagues 4.6 -1.1
@cmd move_npc leagues 7.2 -1.1
NARRATOR: He lifts the spare guitar off the wall.
MAMA DEE [angry]: That's decorative!
@cmd move_npc leagues 1.6 -2.8
@cmd move_npc leagues 1.6 -3.9
NARRATOR: He walks on stage, plugs into Roxy's amp, the one Eddar punched, and plays.
@bgm burn_forever
@fx gold_threads leagues
@cam focus roxy
NARRATOR: It's something no one in Solace Bay has ever heard: a jazz-cathedral guitar line that bends time. Light pours off him in gold threads and finds Spike, Lulu and Roxy.
@fx eye_flash band
NARRATOR: Their eyes flash white. Spike's bass drops in, then Lulu's drums, then Roxy screams into a second lead line that answers his. The Wildfires become something enormous.
@fx vision on
@card The Canticle of Life, Verse 1 of 2
NARRATOR: Red ink on endless scrolls. A city of bells. A crowd singing at sunrise.
STRANGER [vo]: Before the first city, there was the first song, and every living thing was a verse of it. The Rubric wrote it down in red and called it the Canticle.
STRANGER [vo]: And the Canticle says that when the music thins, when the birds forget their tunes and the sea forgets its rhythm, the Scion of Silence will come walking.
NARRATOR: A black stain of quiet creeps across a map. The birds fall still.
STRANGER [vo]: Not an army. Not a storm. A quiet that eats the song from the inside. Steel cannot cut it. Prayer cannot reach it.
STRANGER [vo]: Only one hand may still it: the Champion of All Peoples, the Hero of Legend, named when the Silence wakes.
STRANGER [vo]: So it has been since the world and its lifeblood, the music, began. The Silence rises. The Champion answers. The Champion prevails. Always.
STRANGER [vo]: In every age, the people forgot. They made a party of it, and called it Save the World. And in every age, the Silence came back, to see whether they still meant it.
@fx vision off
@fx gold_threads off
@sfx big_chord
@cam shake
NARRATOR: The song ends on a chord that rattles every bottle in the bar. Silence. Then the whole room cheers, even Mama Dee.
@sfx cheer
@bgm wyvern_live
@cam focus roxy
@emote roxy fire
ROXY [smile]: THAT. That was "Burn Forever"! I wrote that LAST NIGHT, on a napkin, in the bath... never mind where.
ROXY [smile]: It needs TWO lead guitars. We only have one. It was IMPOSSIBLE, and you just FINISHED it, Leagues guy!
LEAGUES: Leagues Soprano.
ROXY: How do I write a song last night that only becomes possible tonight? That's MAGIC.
LEAGUES: Not magic at all. Prophecy. The Canticle tells that a Soprano would open the way for the One to see who he is. Your song was the door, Miss Vega. I only turned the handle.
ROXY [smile]: Okay, the Rex part is still a joke. But play the heat with us. Please. Please, please, please. My hair's doing it again, I'm so excited.
@emote roxy fire
NARRATOR: Her hair is indeed on fire, but in a happy way.
LEAGUES: I would be honoured. But I must go before the bells. I'll meet you there.
REX [smug]: The Hero of All Peoples. Say it again, robe guy. Slower.
MAMA DEE [angry]: It's Hero of LEGEND, you fool!
LEDGER: Entry #2,208: Tonight, Rex Valor was named the Hero of all the world. I wrote his love letters this evening. I suppose I'll write his legend too, and sign it with his name.
@flag p.champion
@end

@scene prologue.screams
# PLOT: Monsters off the docks; Sable walks in and looks at Eddar first; Leagues bows to her; the Bellshell breaks through the front window.
# CHARACTER: Sable's clipped certainty; Rex's oblivious claim; Roxy's fury on behalf of her heat night; Mama Dee herding her people.
@sfx scream
@bgm monster_pulse
NARRATOR: Outside, a scream, then many. Something howls like feedback through a broken speaker. The room tone drains away, and a low, uneasy pulse replaces it.
VOICE: Monsters! They're coming off the docks!
@sfx door
@flag p.sable_in
@cmd enter_npc sable front
@cam focus sable
NARRATOR: The front door swings open. Sable walks in, visor up, looking at only one person in the room: Eddar.
SABLE: So you're the One? The One who'll save all peoples? Let's see, Champion.
REX [smug]: This dweeb? Ha! No, lady with a mask on. I'm the Champion of Champions, or whatever my title is.
@cam focus leagues
LEAGUES: The Champion of All Peoples. The Hero of Legend.
NARRATOR: He gives Sable a small bow, one old order to another. She gives him the smallest nod in return, the way you nod to a priest you find tiresome.
@cam focus mama_dee
MAMA DEE [angry]: Everybody in the back! Now! Gil, put down the beer. ...Fine, bring the beer, just MOVE.
@cmd exit_npc mama_dee left
@cmd exit_npc gil left
@cmd exit_npc spike left
@cmd exit_npc lulu left
@flag p.screams
@cam focus roxy
@emote roxy fire
NARRATOR: Roxy rips her flying-V from its case. Its headstock is an axe blade.
ROXY [angry]: Nobody wrecks my heat night. NOBODY.
@cam focus sable
SABLE: You're the One?
REX [smug]: You got it, doll.
SABLE: Irrelevant. People won't save themselves. Get to it, champions.
@cmd exit_npc sable front
@flag p.sable_gone
@flag p.leagues_gone
NARRATOR: She's gone. When Eddar looks back at the stage, so is Leagues. The alley door is still swinging.
EDDAR: Champions, she said. Plural.
REX [smug]: She meant me twice.
ROXY [angry]: Did that girl just walk into my venue and BOSS me?
EDDAR: Mama Dee's venue.
ROXY [angry]: NOT THE POINT, EDDAR.
@sfx crab_clang
@cam shake
NARRATOR: The front window bows inward.
@sfx glass
@fx shatter window
@flag p.bellshell_in
@cmd enter_npc bellshell window
@cam focus bellshell
NARRATOR: Then it bursts. A crab the size of a car drags itself through the glass. Its shell is shaped like a ship's bell, cracked down one side, and it clangs with every step. It's clanging out of tune.
EDDAR: Wait. Listen to it. It isn't angry. It's in pain.
REX [angry]: Great. It can be in pain AND out of my bar.
ROXY [angry]: It's not your bar either!
@join roxy
@battle bellshell
@end

@scene prologue.bellshell_mercy
# PLOT: The fight ends in mercy: Roxy's furious chord rings true by accident, and the Bellshell answers and goes home to the sea.
# CHARACTER: Roxy's fury and wonder; Eddar's careful uncertainty (he can't know what calms monsters); Rex's fifty-fifty.
@cam focus bellshell
@sfx crab_clang
NARRATOR: The Bellshell pins Roxy against the stage, its cracked bell clanging inches from her face.
ROXY [angry]: Fine! You want NOISE? HERE'S NOISE!
@sfx big_chord
@emote roxy fire
NARRATOR: Roxy slams her guitar in pure fury, and one clean chord rings out.
@sfx bell_true
NARRATOR: The Bellshell stops. Its cracked bell answers with a single true note, the first in weeks. It backs out through the broken window and scuttles toward the sea.
@cmd exit_npc bellshell front
@flag p.bellshell_gone
@cam focus roxy
ROXY: ...Did I just do that?
EDDAR: Something did. I'd not swear it was the chord. Nor would I swear it wasn't.
REX [smug]: Sure. Or Rex scared it. Fifty-fifty.
LEDGER: Entry #2,209: The beast was not cruel. It was a bell that had forgotten its note. I've known men like that. I've been one, most Tuesdays.
@card END OF BUILD 0.3 — THE SIDE ROOM, THE STAIRS AND THE MAIN DRAG COME NEXT
@end

@scene prologue.bellshell_look
# CHARACTER: Eddar listening where others only hear noise.
EDDAR: Every clang is a half-step flat. It isn't roaring. It's trying to find its note and failing, again and again.
@end

@scene prologue.rex_after
# CHARACTER: Rex, newly named, insufferable and still a little bit decent.
@if seen.prologue.rex_after>=1
REX [smug]: Champion of All Peoples. Champion of All... Rex is gonna need a bigger pauldron.
EDDAR: And a smaller head, but one miracle at a time.
@end
@endif
REX [smile]: You see that, Adder? Rex walks in, monster walks out. That's what champions do. It's in the Canticle. Probably.
EDDAR: It's in the Canticle that the monster left. The Canticle is unclear on whose chord it was.
REX: Rex's chord. Spiritually.
@end

@scene prologue.roxy_after
# CHARACTER: Roxy shaken and thrilled at once; the fire and the fear under it.
@if seen.prologue.roxy_after>=1
ROXY: Spike and Lulu are in the back with Mama Dee. Mikey's at home with the twins. He's fine. He's FINE. He has the boots.
EDDAR: He has the boots, and a sister who just out-shouted a bell the size of a car. He's the safest boy in the Bay.
@end
@endif
@emote roxy fire
ROXY [angry]: It wrecked the WINDOW, Eddar. On HEAT NIGHT. If Velvet Kane shows up and the place looks like a shipwreck, I am going to fight the ocean.
EDDAR: I'd back you, Roxy. The ocean's never once been in a fight with you.
@end

@scene prologue.sable
# CHARACTER: Sable doesn't make small talk, and Eddar notices.
SABLE: ...
EDDAR: She looks at me the way one reads a sentence twice, to be sure of its meaning.
@end
